    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f7dbc55_533c7bca",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifi.hal",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T22:58:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The question is what happens on stop failure. Is it similar to start on already started - a nop or something else.\n\nIf stop failure indicates that wasn\u0027t stopped and still running then no need for the callback.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0929b268a331c3a312d76f70a42c092028406427",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f7dbc55_2e15cc52",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifi.hal",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T23:32:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "|onFailure| is used to indicate any fatal errors. If the hal stop fails, then we need to restart the HAL.\n\nSo, |onFailure| should always trigger an invalidation of HIDL objects. Added a comment to clarify that.",
      "parentUuid": "9f7dbc55_533c7bca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "0929b268a331c3a312d76f70a42c092028406427",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f7dbc55_93c3639e",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifiChip.hal",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039103
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T22:58:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this is the case - i.e. leaving the chip in an undetermined state then must tell everyone - not enough to just tell caller (by returning status). Need a callback for failure, or use a special code on reconfigured (ugly).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "0929b268a331c3a312d76f70a42c092028406427",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f7dbc55_2e278cba",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/IWifiChip.hal",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-10-11T23:32:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since this is a fatal error, we should again trigger a |IWifiEventCallback.onFailure| for this as well. \n\nAdded a comment to clarify that.",
      "parentUuid": "9f7dbc55_93c3639e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 18
      },
